// EXPECT: [E132]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 10, Col 14: field 'x' of struct 'S' is bounded by something other than an integer constant ('K' has type 'i32[2]'), so the bound would be silently ignored: a bound is a number, an integer module constant, or another field of the struct (`pos usize <= len`).
// A refinement bound that is a NAME is a sibling (another parameter or field), or an integer
// module constant, folded to its value; anything else is refused at the declaration (F7).
// A table as a field's bound was E132 "names another field".

K = [1, 2]

type S {
    x i32 >= K
}

func main() i32 {
    s = S(7)
    return s.x
}
